# Sejong University Intelligence / Visualization Web App

This repository hosts a static GitHub Pages site for an interactive campus intelligence and visualization dashboard. The project appears to be a front-end application focused on visualizing network, infrastructure, and event data with a map-based UI and timeline-driven analytics.

## Project overview

The app is built as a static web application served from GitHub Pages, with a bundled React/JavaScript front end and several asset directories for fonts, images, and Cesium-based map rendering.

The landing page metadata and bundled assets indicate the site is designed for:

- interactive campus or facility visualization
- event log and timeline exploration
- network / topology analysis
- zone, target, and threat-style intelligence views
- map-driven dashboards with Cesium and Google Maps integrations

## Repository structure

- `index.html` — app entry point and page metadata
- `404.html` — GitHub Pages custom not-found page
- `assets/` — compiled CSS and JavaScript bundles for the application
- `assets/css/` — generated stylesheets
- `assets/js/` — bundled application logic and vendor scripts
- `Font/` — custom local fonts used by the UI
- `image/` — static images used by the site
- `cesium/` — Cesium-related assets and supporting files
- `Console/` — console or internal text files
- `.nojekyll` — disables Jekyll processing on GitHub Pages

## Tech stack

The generated frontend references a production bundle using:

- React
- Material UI (MUI)
- CesiumJS
- Google Maps JavaScript API
- Charting and visualization libraries
- Vite-style bundled assets (the file names suggest a compiled front-end build output)

